    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d233">

                <pb facs="0399" n="303" sameAs="frus:frus1872p1/pg303"/>

                <head>No. 233.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Baxter to Mr. Fish.</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Extract.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Tegucigalpa, Honduras</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1872-05-30"><hi rendition="#italic">May</hi> 30, 1872</date>.
                        (Received July 3.)</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 52.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: To-day the official report is received in
                    Tegucigalpa that on the 27th President Medina attacked Comayagua with the hope
                    to repossess <pb facs="0400" n="304" xml:id="pg304"/> the capital, and that
                    after a battle of many hours he was repulsed with severe loss in killed and
                    wounded, and was forced to retire very much disorganized. This news gives the
                    revolutionists great encouragement for the speedy downfall of President Medina’s
                    government, and the permanent establishment of the provisional government. No
                    information whatever has thus far been received here of the allied armies of
                    Salvador and Guatemala <hi rendition="#italic">supposed</hi> to be in the field,
                    or of <hi rendition="#italic">either</hi> of them, except this division.* * * *
                    * *</p>
                <p>I have, &amp;c,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>HENRY BAXTER.</signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
